From 30cf6af2e116a5653dfc3ce1e3b7883ee41c907a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Rutledge <shawn.rutledge@qt.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:23:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] Update md4c to 0.6.0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Amends d377d1f3a921488525f6e75c850632f559707747 : Qt's definition of
GitHub dialect remains as it was, while md4c has recently added features
that we don't yet support. We need to verify that the new features are
not inadvertently turned on before Qt is ready to handle them, and deal
with the clashing feature flag (0x100000 is for FrontMatter in Qt,
footnotes in md4c). It seems for now that we will not be able to support
footnotes, both because of the clashing flag and because it would be
hard to change the text-editing components to support them; so a test is
added to verify that the markdown footnote syntax is NOT interpreted
specially. Likewise, a test verifies that a markdown "admonition" is
treated as an ordinary block quote for now (but this can be improved
later).

[ChangeLog][Third-Party Code] Updated md4c to version 0.6.0.

Pick-to: 6.5 6.8 6.12 6.12.0
Fixes: QTBUG-148738
Fixes: QTBUG-150636
Fixes: QTBUG-150661
Task-number: QTBUG-149921
